SCOPE NOTE: THIRD-PARTY CONTENT NOT COVERED BY THIS LICENSE
================================================================================

The MIT License above applies to the software authored by this group: the
analyser and its modules, the evaluation and reproduction scripts, the
hand-written benchmark workflows under replication/3_dataset_b/ and
replication/6_dataset_b_extended/, the test cases under testcases/, and the
documentation.

It does NOT apply to the following, which are third-party material collected
from public GitHub repositories and redistributed here only so that the
published results can be independently verified:

  - replication/4_dataset_a_sample/
        300 GitHub Actions workflow files retrieved through the GitHub Search
        API on 5 September 2026, renamed to AXXXX__<original file name>.yml.

  - The release asset dataset_a_corpus_raw.zip
        The 23,995 workflow files returned by the same crawl.

Each of those files remains under the license of the project it came from, and
copyright remains with its original authors. The file name of every sample
records the source repository, so provenance can be traced. They are included
under a research and verification rationale only. If you are the owner of a
repository represented in this corpus and want a file removed, open an issue
and it will be removed.

The baseline tools compared against in the paper, Gitleaks, Zizmor and Poutine,
are not redistributed here. Only their output on the two datasets is stored,
under replication/out/ and replication/out_dsb/.
